{
  "name": "stop-stdin-closed-mid-stream",
  "description": "stdin is closed in the middle of a streamed answer (what the SDK does first when the caller aborts), and the stand-in API never finishes that answer (it starts the stream and then holds the line open): the program writes nothing more and does NOT exit, because it is still waiting for the model call; the driver killed it after 17 seconds. This is not what a closed stdin does to a reply that ends: then the program writes the rest of the turn and its result and exits with code 0 (verify/real.json, s6-stdin-closed-mid-stream-stream-completes and s14-stdin-closed-then-tool).",
  "how": "The real claude 2.1.319 started directly (no SDK) with stdin, stdout and stderr as pipes, in an empty home, with a fake credential, against a loopback stand-in for the Messages API. t is milliseconds from the start of the process.",
